# Environment files — what each one is for.
#
# Copy the relevant block into the named file (all of them are gitignored).
# Every variable says WHY it exists, so a second machine can be set up without
# reading the source.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .env.development.local — read by `npm run dev` and `npm run tauri:dev`
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Points the app at the LOCAL Supabase stack (`npx supabase start`, needs
# Docker Desktop). Development never touches the real server or real people's
# data. These are the stock local values every Supabase install uses; the
# publishable key is printed by `npx supabase status`.
#
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
# VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_...
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .env.production.local — read by `npm run build` and `npm run tauri:build`
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Points release builds at the ONE hosted Supabase project that everyone
# (friends, family, both of your machines) shares. Without it, a release
# build shows "This build isn't connected to a server".
#
# The publishable key is designed to ship inside the app: row-level security
# on the server, not this key, is what keeps each person's data private.
#
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_...
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .env.admin.local — read only by `npm run invite`
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The hosted project's SECRET key, used to manage the invite list. It bypasses
# row-level security, so it lives only on the machine you manage invites
# from. Never give it a VITE_ prefix: Vite inlines every VITE_ variable into
# the built JavaScript, where anyone can read it.
#
# SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=sb_secret_...
